Local Variable Practice

This program demonstrates how to use a local variable in C#.

The program creates a variable called myName. It gets the user’s name from a TextBox and stores it in the variable.

What this code demonstrates:

* Creating a variable
* Using a String
* Getting text from a TextBox
* Storing data in a variable



Int.Parse

Int.Parse Practice

This program demonstrates how to use int.Parse() in C#.

The program gets the number of hours worked from a TextBox. It converts the text into an integer and displays the result in a MessageBox.

What this code demonstrates:

* Integer variables
* Using int.Parse()
* Converting text to an integer
* Using MessageBox



 String Concatenation

String Concatenation Practice

This program demonstrates how to combine two strings in C#.

The program gets the first name and last name from two TextBoxes. It combines them to create a full name and displays it in a Label.

What this code demonstrates:

* String variables
* First name and last name
* Combining strings
* Using TextBox and Label